  "verbalization": "Cocosamide B appears to act as a target for multiple entities, ultimately leading to Thrombopoietin through a series of intermediate targets. The evidence suggests that Cocosamide B interacts with VMRC-LCP, which is a target of several compounds, including methylseleno carboxyethylglutamine and 7-angeloylechinatine, all of which have a shared target of Thrombopoietin. This indicates a potential pathway where Cocosamide B may influence Thrombopoietin through these intermediates. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism involving the modulation of signaling pathways that regulate thrombopoiesis, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a functional link between Cocosamide B and Thrombopoietin, but further experimental validation is needed to confirm the direct or indirect relationship.",
